What's a semi join? why is EXISTS the natual why to write one?

A semi join retunrs rows form the left table when a macthing row exists in the right table. 
Unlike an inner join, it doesn't duplicate left side rows when multiple matches exist. 
we commonly implement it using EXISTS or IN. if we want rows without matches, we use NOT EXISTS, which is an anti-semi-join.
